+# AminGram (Fix 5 / v3.0.5): MVEL 2.5.2 ships a JSR-223 integration
+# (org.mvel2.jsr223.MvelScriptEngine[Factory]) that references
+# javax.script.* classes, which do not exist on Android — R8 fails
+# the release build with "Missing classes detected". The engine
+# never uses the JSR-223 ScriptEngine API (it calls MVEL.eval
+# directly), so this code path is dead on Android.
+-dontwarn javax.script.**
+# AminGram (Fix 7 / v3.0.7): MVEL resolves its optimizer classes BY NAME
+# STRING at runtime (OptimizerFactory static init does
+# ClassLoader.loadClass("org.mvel2.asm.ClassWriter"); the accessor
+# compiler is then instantiated via newInstance()). R8 renamed
+# org.mvel2.** in v59, so the lookup failed and MenuInjector's static
+# init threw "unable to instantiate accessor compiler" — opening any
+# chat crashed (NoClassDefFoundError: MenuInjector). Same failure
+# class: HookGate loads de.robv.android.xposed.XposedBridge (and
+# $HookInfo / $CopyOnWriteSortedSet) via Class.forName — already kept
+# by the M3 block below, so no duplicate line here — and
+# ClassProxyFactory generates DEX at runtime with com.android.dx
+# DexMaker. Upstream exteraless keeps all three; we port the missing
+# ones (mvel2 + dx).
+-keep class org.mvel2.** { *; }
+-dontwarn org.mvel2.**
+-keep class com.android.dx.** { *; }
+-dontwarn com.android.dx.**
