+# AminGram (Fix 12 / v3.0.12): pre-flight sweep (2026-11-17, report
+# verify-scratch/sweep/SWEEP-REPORT-2026-11-17.md) of the full ZwyLib
+# 3.1.0 + MSL 1.1.1 corpus (232 Java refs, AST-based) found the gaps
+# below against the v63 DEX. P0: ZwyLib's ui/uikit.py:18 does
+# `from org.telegram.messenger.utils import ViewOutlineProviderImpl`
+# (used at uikit.py:394, boundsWithRoundRect) - the class exists in the
+# 13.2.2 base but R8 renamed it (descriptor count 0 in v63), and Fix 8's
+# `-keep class org.telegram.messenger.*` is single-level and does NOT
+# cover the messenger.utils subpackage. Without this keep the next
+# device test fails exactly like Fix 9 (import zwylib fails, MSL falls
+# to RecursiveMock, NameError: SettingEntry at line 119). Single class,
+# not the whole subpackage: the sweep found this as the ONLY gap in
+# messenger.utils, and the class's anonymous inner classes (BOUNDS_OVAL
+# etc.) are referenced only from inside the class itself, so they need
+# no name keep. Lesson: a single-level -keep does not cover
+# subpackages - enumerate subpackages too. P1-1: MSL's embedded DEX
+# reflectively reads three fields to live-refresh open Settings
+# screens (SettingsSyncManager): LaunchActivity.instance (public
+# static, LaunchActivity.java:393), LaunchActivity.actionBarLayout
+# (public, :312), SettingsActivity.listView (private
+# UniversalRecyclerView, SettingsActivity.java:162). All three were
+# renamed in v63; the failure is swallowed (logged, no crash), so the
+# toggle applies but the open screen stays stale until Settings is
+# reopened. P1-2: MSL DEX lambdas return kotlin/Unit; the app DEX has
+# no kotlin.Unit or DefaultConstructorMarker (R8 stripped them as
+# unused). Likely benign (the 8 setters return void) but the keeps cost
+# nothing; on-device toggle testing is still the proof.
+-keep class org.telegram.messenger.utils.ViewOutlineProviderImpl { *; }
+-keepclassmembers class org.telegram.ui.LaunchActivity { public static org.telegram.ui.LaunchActivity instance; public org.telegram.ui.ActionBar.ActionBarLayout actionBarLayout; }
+-keepclassmembers class org.telegram.ui.SettingsActivity { private org.telegram.ui.Components.UniversalRecyclerView listView; }
+-keep class kotlin.Unit { *; }
+-keep class kotlin.jvm.internal.DefaultConstructorMarker { *; }
+# AminGram (Fix 13 / v3.0.13): nested classes are separate classes in R8.
+# A single-class keep (-keep class org.telegram.ui.GroupCreateActivity
+# { *; }, Fix 11) keeps that class and its members but NOT its nested
+# classes, so ZwyLib's ui/navigation.py:100
+# `class _PickerDelegate(dynamic_proxy(GroupCreateActivity.GroupCreateActivityDelegate))`
+# died on device with "AttributeError: type object 'GroupCreateActivity'
+# has no attribute 'GroupCreateActivityDelegate'" - the interface exists
+# in the 13.2.2 base (GroupCreateActivity.java:164) but its v65 DEX
+# descriptor count is 0. Package-wildcard keeps DO cover nested classes
+# (proven: NotificationCenter$NotificationCenterDelegate and
+# AlertDialog$OnButtonClickListener survive via the messenger.*/ActionBar.*
+# wildcards), so these three use the $* wildcard form, scoped to three
+# already-kept parents - it also covers ContactsAddActivityDelegate
+# (GroupCreateActivity.java:168, no current lookup) and any other nested
+# class of these parents. Re-enumeration (AST-based, Parent.Nested
+# attribute access + dynamic_proxy + jclass("...$...") across the SDK,
+# ZwyLib 3.1.0 and MSL, checked by exact descriptor match against the
+# v65 DEX) found FOUR missing nested classes, not three: the brief's
+# three below, PLUS UItem$UItemFactory - ZwyLib's ui/plugin_cells.py:116
+# calls UItem.UItemFactory.setup(...) at import time (api.py:87 imports
+# navigation before api.py:157 imports plugin_cells, so the delegate
+# error surfaced first, but the factory call would have failed next).
+# UItemFactory is `public static abstract class UItemFactory`
+# (UItem.java:845) with `setup(UItemFactory)` (:846); descriptor 0 in
+# v65. All four exist in the 13.2.2 base. Present already, no action:
+# NotificationCenter$NotificationCenterDelegate, R$raw, R$string,
+# AlertDialog$Builder/$OnButtonClickListener, Theme$ThemeInfo,
+# BulletinFactory$FileType, StarGiftSheet$PageTransition,
+# SendMessagesHelper$SendMessageParams, SharedConfig$ProxyInfo,
+# Utilities$Callback/2/3/Return, TLRPC$* (tgnet.** keep),
+# CustomSetting$Factory, PluginsConstants$Xposed,
+# PluginsController$InstallCallback. UItem's reflectively-read fields
+# `factories`/`factoryInstances` (plugin_cells.py:106-107) are present
+# under their real names in v65 - no field keep needed. Lesson: a keep
+# list built from from-imports + jclass strings misses Parent.Nested
+# attribute access - enumerate that pattern too.
+-keep class org.telegram.ui.GroupCreateActivity$* { *; }
+-keep class org.telegram.ui.DialogsActivity$* { *; }
+-keep class org.telegram.ui.Components.UItem$* { *; }
+-keep class app.exteraless.plugins.** { *; }
+-keep class com.exteragram.messenger.** { *; }
 # AminGram (M0): class names plugins and DEX code resolve by string
 # (keepnames only - members are audited per target in M3).
 -keepnames class org.telegram.ui.SettingsActivity
